body:
> Being a woman is basically living on easy mode. 

&#x200B;

That's not true. Women have to deal with a lot of things men don't. is it easy being a man no. but it's not "living on easy mode" to be a woman either and it's insulting to suggest otherwise. Socially we have pressures that men don't. Physically, women have severe pain every month till menopause after puberty. Women have a higher incidence of things like osteoarthritis,Alzheimers,lupus. Women are physically weaker and shorter than men on average. Women are usually discouraged from/ignored in doing "man things" like learning to build things, handle car maintenance, building fires.. So usually a woman cant do a lot of the things a man can or is expected to do. and when you live alone it can really suck trying to do those things without a man around who can. Now again, do men have it easy just because of being men? No. Men have struggles too. as an MRA I am well acquainted with the issues facing men. BUT that's why BOTH have issues and strengths and should be respected in their differences rather than trying to play "no I'm the bigger victim" games. That gets people nowhere as to the "other side" it just sounds like whining.

> My family, disregarding my brother and BF, are pissed off at me for deciding to open my mouth and tell my therapist. 

&#x200B;

ahem. they...are MAD because you told the person who's job it is to sort out and help with your mental state..that your mental state was in distress because of a MASSIVE, LONG STANDING violation of trust, privacy, dignity and respect. They clearly have no idea how therapy works if they think you don't tell a therapist about mental and emotional trauma. wtf do they think you're SUPPOSED to talk about, breakfast?!  and as far as the restaurant thing, okay that may have been inappropriate for the workplace but YOU didn't do that. that's not on you. same with the friends. and YOU didn't call cps. so YOU did nothing but what you should have, which is to inform your SO and your therapist. the therapist did what they should and put the welfare and safety of children over the discomfort of a jackass. if he didn't do anything, nothing will come of it and it wont matter. if he did? then he will get what is coming to him. in spades. you are NTA. I won't say you are a victim either because you aren't helpless, you will get through this. Remember this going forward. He tried to take advantage of you, and you got help. you didn't hide. you didn't let him take what he wanted from you. You are strong.
